WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.700
A minimal handler records intent and returns.

2
00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:11.720
That intent may be shutdown requested, reload requested, child status should be checked, or diagnostic state should be noted in a limited way.

3
00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:14.540
The handler should not try to complete the whole operation.

4
00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:19.920
Its job is to bridge from asynchronous interruption to a safer part of the program.

5
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:24.440
Simple flags are a common pattern when used with the right constraints.

6
00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:31.100
A handler can set a flag of a type appropriate for signal communication, and the main loop can check that flag at controlled points.

7
00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:43.280
The main code then performs the real work: stop accepting new requests, drain queues, close resources, write logs, remove temporary files, or exit with the intended status.

8
00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:49.560
Some programs need a notification channel so a blocking loop can wake up promptly.

9
00:00:49.660 --> 00:01:00.060
A self-pipe style pattern is one high-level example: the handler performs a minimal signal-safe notification, and the event loop handles the full transition when it wakes.

10
00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:06.800
The important idea is not the specific mechanism; it is that complex logic remains in ordinary control flow.

11
00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:10.040
Shared state needs careful boundaries.

12
00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:13.900
The handler should touch only state designed for signal communication.

13
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:18.160
Normal code should read and reset that state in a predictable way.

14
00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:27.220
If a signal can arrive during initialization or shutdown, the program should define what the flag means before setup is complete and after cleanup has begun.

15
00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:30.460
The design should also be easy to review.

16
00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:33.040
Name the handler's limited responsibility.

17
00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:35.700
Document which state it can touch.

18
00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:39.800
Keep the transition from signal request to mainline action clear.

19
00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:45.260
When the handler is intentionally boring, the rest of the program becomes easier to reason about under interruption.
